 "drivingQuestion": "Which books fall under 'external books', and why would ben Sira be among them?",
 "outcome": "inconclusive",
 "outcomeNote": "the unit ends mid-argument; Abaye's suggestion is tested in the following sugya",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "sanhedrin.100b.3",
   "daf": "100b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "רַבִּי עֲקִיבָא אוֹמֵר אַף הַקּוֹרֵא בַּסְּפָרִים הַחִיצוֹנִים וְכוּ' תָּנָא בְּסִפְרֵי מִינִים רַב יוֹסֵף אָמַר בְּסֵפֶר בֶּן סִירָא נָמֵי אָסוּר לְמִיקְרֵי אֲמַר לֵיהּ אַבָּיֵי מַאי טַעְמָא אִילֵּימָא מִשּׁוּם דִּכְתִב [בֵּיהּ] לָא תִּינְטוֹשׁ גִּילְדָּנָא מֵאוּדְנֵיהּ דְּלָא לֵיזִיל מַשְׁכֵיהּ לַחֲבָלָא אֶלָּא צְלִי יָתֵיהּ בְּנוּרָא וְאֵיכוֹל בֵּיהּ תַּרְתֵּין גְּרִיצִים",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «Rabbi Akiva says: Also one who reads external literature» has no share in the World-to-Come. The Sages «taught» in a baraita: This is a reference to reading «books of heretics. Rav Yosef says: It is also prohibited to read the book of ben Sira,» due to its problematic content. «Abaye said to» Rav Yosef: «What is the reason» that it is prohibited to read the book of ben Sira? «If we say» that it is prohibited «due to» the fact «that» ben Sira «wrote in it: Do not flay the skin of the fish from its ear, so that its skin does not go to ruin, but roast it on the fire and eat with it two loaves of bread,» and you believe it to be nonsense, that is not a sufficient reason."
  }
 ],
